{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410846-how-much-infrastructure-paperclips-did-the-virtual-adapts-and-etherites-abscond-with","id":1410846,"title":"How Much Infrastructure/Paperclips did the Virtual Adapts and Etherites Abscond with?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-28T07:31:51-07:00","id":1410846,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How Much Infrastructure/Paperclips did the Virtual Adapts and Etherites Abscond with?","content":"So when the Virtual Adepts (they were what the Difference Engineers at the Time right?) and the Sons of Ether (they were Electrodyne Engineers at the time right) quite how much sheer stuff did they yoink/sabotage when they went out to get a pack of smokes and never returned? Like design, production, and distribution of Devices and Extraordinary Citizens is a group effort but then all of a sudden a rather sizeable chunk of the Union stuffs as much staplers, coffee mugs, and material fabricators in their labcoats as they can and then promptly and quietly cheeses it. Like wouldn't this be an insanely substantial setback if you also include the compromised security and sabotage? How close together was their defection again? Technocratic History wasn't my strong suite.<br /> <br /> And with all this as precedent how much of the Infrastructure, Resources, Manpower (Mortal, Robots, Clones, ect) would be compromised when the Void Engineers eventually go AWOL? And if a pan Convention Group like the Friends of Courage and Avalon team up and ditch how much of the Union is left and how would they avoid the civil war that follows from the resource vacuum and disagreements? Would new Conventions inevitably form to fill the need? How quickly? Would some of the staying Conventions split into Multiple Conventions to fill in the Gaps, like wasn't the Old NWO multiple conventions based on Education and Philosophy ect back in the day?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T08:39:39-07:00","id":1410850,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking the etherites took every that didn't conform to the technocracy newly defined theories of science, the crown jewel being Victoria Station on the moon. <br /> <br /> The VA's however didn't steal as much as they scorched the earth on their, setting off timed sabotages that were years in the making. Much like how the 2nd edition VE's had planned to do on their exit from earth sphere prior to the avatar storm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T15:52:08-07:00","id":1410896,"title":"","content":"The irony, IMHO, is that the VEs <i>did</i> jump ship when the Avatar Storm struck \u2014 at least, those of them who were inclined to did. Those who remain cover for this with \u201cwe were decimated by the Storm\u201d; but the truth of the matter is that the old-style wanderlust-driven VEs, for the most part, didn't die; they Void Adapted and went off exploring, never to be seen again \u2014 we hope. Because if they <i>do</i> return, it will most likely be as allies of the Deep Universe's natives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T21:12:14-07:00","id":1410942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410846-how-much-infrastructure-paperclips-did-the-virtual-adapts-and-etherites-abscond-with?p=1410896#post1410896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The irony, IMHO, is that the VEs <i>did</i> jump ship when the Avatar Storm struck \u2014 at least, those of them who were inclined to did. Those who remain cover for this with \u201cwe were decimated by the Storm\u201d; but the truth of the matter is that the old-style wanderlust-driven VEs, for the most part, didn't die; they Void Adapted and went off exploring, never to be seen again \u2014 we hope. Because if they <i>do</i> return, it will most likely be as allies of the Deep Universe's natives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohh I really like this take!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}